WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.545
Sports and Games.

2
00:00:01.825 --> 00:00:06.198
Day 46 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:07.948 --> 00:00:08.972
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.252 --> 00:00:16.676
Today's goal: join a game, book a court, talk with teammates, and chat about cricket and other sports with colleagues and neighbours.

5
00:00:18.026 --> 00:00:18.879
Part 1.

6
00:00:19.159 --> 00:00:20.119
Key words.

7
00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:22.735
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:23.015 --> 00:00:44.561
Word or phrase, and Meaning. court or ground or turf or pitch: where you play. book a slot or court booking: reserve time to play. team or captain or opponent or substitute: people in a game. score or win or lose or draw or tie: results. serve or rally or smash (badminton): badminton terms. bat or

9
00:00:44.841 --> 00:00:56.148
bowl or wicket or boundary or over (cricket): cricket terms. warm up or injury or cramp: before playing or getting hurt. match or tournament or league: competitions.

10
00:00:57.498 --> 00:00:58.373
Part 2.

11
00:00:58.653 --> 00:00:59.869
Questions you'll ask.

12
00:01:01.119 --> 00:01:02.207
Can I join you?

13
00:01:02.487 --> 00:01:03.937
Do you need one more player?

14
00:01:04.217 --> 00:01:05.540
How do I book a court?

15
00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.889
Is it ₹ per hour or per person?

16
00:01:08.169 --> 00:01:09.727
Do you play every weekend?

17
00:01:10.007 --> 00:01:10.860
What time?

18
00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.399
Doubles or singles?

19
00:01:12.679 --> 00:01:14.897
Whose serve is it? / What's the score?

20
00:01:15.177 --> 00:01:16.927
Did you watch the match last night?

21
00:01:17.207 --> 00:01:19.063
Who do you support in the IPL?

22
00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:21.309
Part 3.

23
00:01:21.589 --> 00:01:24.341
Conversation 1: joining a badminton group.

24
00:01:25.591 --> 00:01:27.617
Here is how the conversation goes.

25
00:01:27.897 --> 00:01:28.623
Hi!

26
00:01:28.903 --> 00:01:30.823
Do you play here every Saturday?

27
00:01:31.103 --> 00:01:32.703
Yes, from 7 to 9.

28
00:01:32.983 --> 00:01:35.073
We're a group from the apartments nearby.

29
00:01:35.353 --> 00:01:36.740
Could I join you?

30
00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.263
I haven't played in a while, but I'd love to start again.

31
00:01:40.543 --> 00:01:41.204
Sure!

32
00:01:41.484 --> 00:01:43.105
We usually play doubles.

33
00:01:43.385 --> 00:01:44.943
We split the court booking.

34
00:01:45.223 --> 00:01:47.548
It's 150 rupeesper person.

35
00:01:48.898 --> 00:01:50.498
The conversation continues.

36
00:01:50.778 --> 00:01:51.866
That's fine.

37
00:01:52.146 --> 00:01:54.002
Do I need my own racket?

38
00:01:54.282 --> 00:01:55.925
Bring your own if you have one.

39
00:01:56.205 --> 00:01:57.613
We provide shuttles.

40
00:01:57.893 --> 00:01:58.639
Great.

41
00:01:58.919 --> 00:02:00.626
I'll come next Saturday.

42
00:02:00.906 --> 00:02:02.570
Is there a WhatsApp group?

43
00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.898
Yes, give me your number and I'll add you.

44
00:02:05.178 --> 00:02:10.447
It's 98450 12345.

45
00:02:10.727 --> 00:02:11.965
Thanks a lot!

46
00:02:13.315 --> 00:02:14.232
Part 4.

47
00:02:14.512 --> 00:02:16.987
Conversation 2: cricket chat at work.

48
00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:20.263
Here is how the conversation goes.

49
00:02:20.543 --> 00:02:22.463
Did you watch the match last night?

50
00:02:22.743 --> 00:02:23.469
Yes!

51
00:02:23.749 --> 00:02:24.879
What a finish.

52
00:02:25.159 --> 00:02:27.933
I couldn't believe they chased 190.

53
00:02:28.213 --> 00:02:29.983
That last over was amazing.

54
00:02:30.263 --> 00:02:31.757
Two sixes in a row!

55
00:02:32.037 --> 00:02:32.975
I know.

56
00:02:33.255 --> 00:02:36.690
I thought they'd lost after the third wicket fell so early.

57
00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:38.293
Who do you support?

58
00:02:39.643 --> 00:02:41.243
The conversation continues.

59
00:02:41.523 --> 00:02:42.888
Chennai, always.

60
00:02:43.168 --> 00:02:46.539
But I don't mind which team wins as long as it's a good match.

61
00:02:46.819 --> 00:02:48.035
What about you?

62
00:02:48.315 --> 00:02:49.403
Bengaluru.

63
00:02:49.683 --> 00:02:51.539
Maybe this is finally our year!

64
00:02:51.819 --> 00:02:52.971
Ha, maybe.

65
00:02:53.251 --> 00:02:56.579
Shall we watch the final together at the café downstairs?

66
00:02:56.859 --> 00:02:58.011
Great idea.

67
00:02:58.291 --> 00:02:59.635
Let's ask the team.

68
00:03:00.985 --> 00:03:01.945
Part 5.

69
00:03:02.225 --> 00:03:03.078
In the game.

70
00:03:04.328 --> 00:03:08.083
Good shot! / Well played! / Unlucky! / Nice try!

71
00:03:08.363 --> 00:03:09.771
Yours! / Mine!

72
00:03:10.051 --> 00:03:11.288
(who takes the shot).

73
00:03:11.568 --> 00:03:12.805
Was that in or out?

74
00:03:13.085 --> 00:03:14.493
Let's play one more game.

75
00:03:14.773 --> 00:03:16.160
Good game, everyone.

76
00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.827
Same time next week?

77
00:03:19.177 --> 00:03:20.115
Part 6.

78
00:03:20.395 --> 00:03:21.313
Practice.

79
00:03:22.563 --> 00:03:27.149
Tell someone about your favourite sport: what you play, how often, where, and with whom.

80
00:03:28.499 --> 00:03:29.438
Part 7.

81
00:03:29.718 --> 00:03:30.763
Speak today.

82
00:03:32.013 --> 00:03:33.571
Start a sports conversation:

83
00:03:33.851 --> 00:03:36.517
Did you watch the match? or Do you play any sport?

84
00:03:36.797 --> 00:03:39.891
Learn 5 encouraging phrases to use in a game.

85
00:03:41.241 --> 00:03:42.777
That's the end of this lesson.

86
00:03:43.057 --> 00:03:47.729
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

87
00:03:48.009 --> 00:03:54.110
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

